  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 139 AM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThe previously mentioned upper trough is expected to continue to \napproach the area over the weekend and move into the southern Plains \nearly next week. Models also show a cold front moving across the \narea early next week. This system will bring a chance for showers \nand maybe some storms starting this weekend and continuing into next \nweek with the earliest and highest chances over western portions of \nthe fa. The amount of moisture with this system does not look as \nabundant so rainfall amounts are not expected to be as high as the \nlast couple of rain events the fa has experienced but some locations \nin western parts of the area may see rainfall totals of 1-1.5 \ninches.\n\nTemperatures will remain warm and above average through the weekend \nwith highs in the 70s to low 80s. Temperatures are then expected to \ncool early next week due to the cold front, clouds, and rain with \nhighs in the 60s and some 70s.",
